---
// Generated from the product OPERATOR manual's own symptom table.
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import docs from '../../generated/docs.json';
const mono = (s) => s.replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>');
---
<Docs title="Troubleshooting · KeepState docs" description="Symptoms, what they mean, and what to do, synced from the operator manual.">
  <h1>Troubleshooting</h1>
  <p>
    <code>ks doctor</code> is the first move, always: it is the executable
    form of every hazard this project has hit, and every gate calls it
    first. The table is synced from the operator manual.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>What it means</th><th>What to do</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {docs.trouble.map((t) => (
        <tr>
          <td set:html={mono(t.symptom)} />
          <td set:html={mono(t.meaning)} />
          <td set:html={mono(t.action)} />
        </tr>
      ))}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Stuck past that? The product's blocked protocol applies to humans too:
    after three genuinely different failed hypotheses, stop and write down
    the symptom, the hypotheses, and the evidence. Then
    <a href="/contact">send it to us</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
